PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Key facts preserved: X-coalition (6 voters incl. voter 1) share {x1,x2,x3}, size=3*(n/k) so ℓ=3 EJR requires ≥1 voter in group gets |A_i ∩ W|≥3; Y-coalition (4 voters) share {y4,y5,y6}, size=2*(n/k) so ℓ=2 requires ≥1 gets ≥2. All EJR committees must satisfy both (plus ℓ=1). 

Disagreement: A supporters claim [2,4] feasible (e.g., W={x1,x2,y1,z3,y4} gives voter 1 exactly 4); H supporters claim only [2,3] (Y-coalition forces 2 y-reps, so 4 from voter 1 leaves at most 1 seat and violates Y). 

Error correction: A examples fail Y ℓ=2 (only 1 y-rep, no Y-voter reaches 2). Feasible W achieving 3 for voter 1 exist (3x + 2y or 2x + y1 + 2y). Cannot drop below 2 (violates X ℓ=3). Thus range exactly [2,3] (H). No unresolved issues remain.}

